            "question": "What is considered a defect?",
            "answer": "<p>A product may be considered defective if it shows physical damage upon unboxing (such as cracks, dents, or breakage not caused after delivery), incorrect or missing items, or ink flow issues on unused pens after proper priming. Manufacturing defects that affect usability may also qualify. Minor marks from manufacturing or packaging are not considered defects.</p>",
            "plus_icon": "<svg width=\"24\" height=\"24\" viewbox=\"0 0 24 24\" fill=\"none\" xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\"><path d=\"M12 5V19M5 12H19\" stroke=\"#931932\" stroke-width=\"2\" stroke-linecap=\"round\"></path></svg>",
